// The Monday onboarding, with Pan Zbigniew and Ryszard. Ryszard teaches the Intern to fake Tasks.
// A line tagged #speaker:intern is the Intern's. A line tagged #speaker:ryszard is Ryszard's.
// Every other line is Pan Zbigniew's.
// This is Ryszard's Monday Conversation too, so he has no Monday knot.
// It is always Monday and Mundane here, so no line branches on tier().
// The Intern does not know the Factions yet, so no line names one.
// The last line sets the "onboarded" flag. Without it, Continue replays the onboarding.

=== onboarding ===
Welcome, welcome! Our newest team member. What a wonderful Monday this is. #id:onboarding.onboarding.1
Biooro. Listening to your body, one flush at a time. Isn't that lovely? #id:onboarding.onboarding.2
Thank you, Pan Zbigniew. I'm happy to be here. #speaker:intern #id:onboarding.onboarding.3
Customers send us feedback moments. We turn each one into a happy ending. #id:onboarding.onboarding.4
Ryszard will show you how we work. Nineteen years with us! An inspiration. #id:onboarding.onboarding.5
Welcome to Customer Complaints. We regret any inconvenience. #speaker:ryszard #id:onboarding.onboarding.6
* [Where do I start? #id:onboarding.onboarding.7]
    You'll get more Tasks than the day has hours. Everyone does. #speaker:ryszard #id:onboarding.onboarding.8
* [Nineteen years. That's a long time. #id:onboarding.onboarding.9]
    Nineteen years. Three case closure awards. I've read maybe four cases. #speaker:ryszard #id:onboarding.onboarding.10
-
Here's the secret. You don't do a Task. You fake it. #speaker:ryszard #id:onboarding.onboarding.11
Tick the box. Paste Template 4. "Thank you for your patience." One hour, done. #speaker:ryszard #id:onboarding.onboarding.12
* [Doesn't anyone check? #id:onboarding.onboarding.13]
    Sometimes it comes back two days later. Bigger. By then you've had lunch. #speaker:ryszard #id:onboarding.onboarding.14
* [That sounds efficient. #id:onboarding.onboarding.15]
    Efficient. That's what it says on my second award. #speaker:ryszard #id:onboarding.onboarding.16
-
Wonderful! Learning from the best already. Ryszard closes more cases than anyone. #id:onboarding.onboarding.17
Remember, every Task is an opportunity. Every single one. #id:onboarding.onboarding.18
I'll remember that. #speaker:intern #id:onboarding.onboarding.19
~ set_flag("onboarded")
-> END
